##
    A division the compiler cannot see.

    This program compiles. Dividing by a literal zero is refused before it runs, but a
    divisor that arrives in a variable can only be found out at the moment of division, so
    this one throws.
##

shared model Program
    function Main()
        integer[] divisors = {4, 2, 0};

        loop each d in divisors
            Console.WriteLine("100 / " + d + " = " + 100 / d);
        end loop
    end function
end model
